    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This is the Verilog-A Code for RRAM Compact Model. We develop the Verilog-A RRAM compact model taking into account the statistical variability of filament evolution. A methodology to systematically calibrate the model parameters with experimental data is developed and validated with a broad set of DC characteristics from a variety of RRAM devices such as TiOX/HfOX bilayer RRAM and HfOx RRAM with Al-doping devices. In addition to the DC switching characteristics, this model also captures the AC programing transient current behavior, conductance modulation during RESET, and SET stochastic switching under weak programming conditions. The agreement between the simulated and measured data suggests that this physics-based compact model can be used for circuit simulations to guide the analysis and optimization of various circuit and system designs involving RRAM.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
